<blockquote>
<p><strong>Rumour / unconfirmed:</strong> Wikipedia mentions reports from “industry sources” of a PC release in Q1 2027. Rockstar has announced nothing. Source: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Theft_Auto_VI" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Theft_Auto_VI</a></p>
</blockquote>
<p>![platform chart with ticks and crosses](TODO: image:platforms-step-1 — diagram, our own art: a grid of PS5, PS5 Pro, Series X|S, Xbox One (cloud), PS4, PC with ticks, cloud icon and crosses)
<em>Caption: Diagram. Where GTA 6 runs on launch day.</em></p>
<h2 id="frame-rate-and-picture" tabindex="-1">Frame rate and picture</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>30 FPS</strong> is the target on all consoles. Rockstar: “targeting 30 frames per second”.</li>
<li><strong>No 40 or 60 FPS mode</strong> is announced.</li>
<li><strong>Resolution:</strong> not announced.</li>
<li><strong>PS5 Pro:</strong> PSSR and ray-traced shadows.</li>
<li><strong>Xbox Cloud Gaming:</strong> uses <strong>Xbox Series S graphics settings</strong>. Rockstar says internet speed and other things can change how it plays.</li>
<li><strong>Remote Play:</strong> supported on PlayStation and Xbox.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="how-xbox-one-players-stream-gta-6" tabindex="-1">How Xbox One players stream GTA 6</h2>
<ol>
<li>Press the <strong>Xbox button</strong> on your controller.</li>
<li>Open the <strong>Microsoft Store</strong> and buy <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong> (Standard or Ultimate). Xbox says the game <strong>must be purchased separately</strong>.</li>
<li>Starting <strong>11 Nov</strong>, in supported markets, you can also buy cloud playtime to stream supported games <strong>without Game Pass</strong> (Xbox Wire).</li>
<li>At <strong>1 AM ET on 19 Nov</strong>, open the game from <strong>My games &amp; apps</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>Exact menu names for cloud games are not in Xbox’s announcement. Check them on your console. Availability and prices vary by country and device.</p>
<p>![Xbox Cloud Gaming start screen for GTA VI](TODO: image:platforms-step-2 — menu screen, Xbox: GTA VI in My games &amp; apps with the cloud-play option)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. Starting the cloud version on Xbox.</em></p>
<h2 id="languages" tabindex="-1">Languages</h2>
<p>Voice is in <strong>English only</strong>. Text is in English, French, German, Italian, Korean, Polish, Portuguese (Brazil), Russian, Simplified Chinese, Spanish (Mexico), Spanish (Spain) and Traditional Chinese (PlayStation support). <strong>Slovenian and Croatian are not listed.</strong></p>
<p>![language list graphic](TODO: image:platforms-step-3 — diagram, our own art: the 12 text languages and the one voice language)
<em>Caption: Diagram. The languages GTA 6 supports on PlayStation.</em></p>
<h2 id="faq" tabindex="-1">FAQ</h2>
<h3 id="is-gta-6-coming-to-pc" tabindex="-1">Is GTA 6 coming to PC?</h3>
<p>Not announced. Only an unconfirmed report mentions Q1 2027.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-play-gta-6-on-ps4" tabindex="-1">Can I play GTA 6 on PS4?</h3>
<p>No.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-play-gta-6-on-xbox-one" tabindex="-1">Can I play GTA 6 on Xbox One?</h3>
<p>Only by streaming with Xbox Cloud Gaming from 1 AM ET on 19 November.</p>
<h3 id="does-gta-6-run-at-60-fps" tabindex="-1">Does GTA 6 run at 60 FPS?</h3>
<p>No. The target is 30 FPS on every console.</p>
